From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lusoris <lusoris@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/23] fix(qsv): budget udu_sei per picture on hevc_qsv and
 h264_qsv

With udu_sei=1, hevc_qsv and h264_qsv handed the runtime every
SEI_UNREGISTERED entry whole. Larger payloads damage the encoded access
unit: no picture of a hevc_qsv stream decodes (a 4 091-byte payload is
enough) and the encode fails from about 11 KB; the h264_qsv encode
fails from about 42 KB. A Pelorus analyze blob at 1080p with
32-pixel cells (12 424 bytes) hit it on hevc_qsv.

The limit is per picture, not per payload: the sum of the
mfxPayload.BufSize values (SEI message type, size bytes and payload)
passed in one mfxEncodeCtrl. h264_qsv also counts the emulation
prevention bytes of the payloads. Per picture budget:

- hevc_qsv: 4 040 bytes. The runtime damages the picture past 4 107.
- h264_qsv: 40 960 bytes. The encode fails past about 42 420.

The payloads the stock A/53 callback already queued are charged first.
Each SEI_UNREGISTERED entry, in frame order, is then:

- fits: written whole;
- a Pelorus blob that does not fit: written without the per-cell maps
  appended after its sections (every scalar stays, each map offset and
  size is zero, the ABI's absent map), as hevc_nvenc does (ADR-0181);
- anything else that does not fit: not written.

QSV writes a Pelorus blob in its plain form; the zero-free carrier is
for NVENC. The first stripped blob and the first dropped payload are
warnings, later ones verbose, and the totals are a warning at close. The
budget arithmetic is libavcodec/pelorus_sei_fit_qsv.h, built on
pelorus_sei_fit.h from patch 0022, and tested by the Pelorus fast suite.

Measured on an Arc A380 (iHD 26.3.5, vpl-gpu-rt 26.3.5, libvpl 2.17.0),
at 640x360, 1920x1080 and 3840x2160 alike. Depends on patches 0019 and
0022.

Known issue, not fixed here: h264_qsv with udu_sei can crash
intermittently inside Intel's QSV runtime, more often with larger
payloads. It reproduces with stock FFmpeg, so Pelorus does not cause it
and the budget does not prevent it.
---
 libavcodec/pelorus_sei_fit_qsv.h | 133 ++++++++++++++++++++
 libavcodec/qsvenc.c              |  89 +++++++++++--
 libavcodec/qsvenc.h              |   2 +
 3 files changed, 212 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/pelorus_sei_fit_qsv.h b/libavcodec/pelorus_sei_fit_qsv.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..8c5e56e74bcde9b8dcd2e599d9ae40104c89a114
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libavcodec/pelorus_sei_fit_qsv.h
@@ -0,0 +1,133 @@
+/*
+ * Copyright 2026 Lusoris
+ *
+ * This file is part of FFmpeg.
+ *
